en:
"...I agree with {a}, myself."
It was Arai who said it, in a low mutter.
This time, Iwashita glared at Arai.{p}

A girl was standing in front of the door.
"...What's with you? Who are you?"
Shindo eyed her up and down.{p}

When she heard my answer, she smiled happily and ran over to me.
"Good for you.
You're still alive."{p}

"I'll tell you the seventh story.
Before the seventh one comes."
Everyone's eyes turned to her at once.{p}

"The seventh one's coming?
For real?"
Even Shindo seemed interested.{p}

"...If even one person goes home, someone will die for sure.
So you can't go home.
We have to break the curse."{p}

"Hey, {a}.
If you promise to marry me, I'll save you.
I'll tell you the seventh story."{p}

"...All right.
We only just met today, but I feel like this meeting was meant to be.
If you'll have me, I'd be glad to."{p}

"Okay then, I'll tell it."
With that, Motoki settled back into her seat.
Even the bunch who had been laughing a moment ago fell silent, like a receding wave.{p}

...Scary story, huh?
And that's the end of my story.
Thanks for all your hard work.{p}

"...I'd say it was that hysterical girlfriend he was going out with.
From what you told us, she sounds like she might do anything once she got desperate enough."
When I answered, Motoki nodded to herself again and again.{p}

"Don't talk crap!
Why the hell would he come?!"
Shindo suddenly raised his voice.{p}

"...Oh?
Shindo, you know Kanda?"
Motoki put on a big show of surprise. Whether it was real or an act, I couldn't tell.{p}

"You killed him, didn't you?!
Shouldn't you take responsibility and be the sacrifice, Iwashita?!"
Shindo, both hands shoved in his pockets and his legs sprawled out lazily, glared at Iwashita.{p}

"Motoki!"
I cried out without thinking, but she didn't respond.
She was unconscious, as if someone had taken her over.{p}

Kazama put on that peculiar grin of his and said,
"Admit it, everyone, my scary story was the scariest, wasn't it?"
Well, since the gathering was ending without incident, everyone just smiled even at Kazama's nonsense.{p}

Everyone here seemed perfectly satisfied, even without hearing a seventh story.
The scary stories themselves were a kind of thank-you for coming.
And everyone was starting to get ready to leave.{p}

"Hey, you're {b} {a}, aren't you?"
Motoki asked again.
...Should I really just answer her honestly here?{p}

"But if the seventh person is coming, let's wait for them."
That's what I said.
If the seventh person really is coming, I'd really like that person to be the one who tells the seventh story.{p}

"No!
Then there'd be no point in my coming here.
I absolutely have to tell the seventh story before the seventh one arrives!"{p}

"I understand.
I'll tell Grandma myself.
That I can't marry you, {a}..."{p}

"It's okay. I'll protect you.
The grandma who went into your mouth, {a}, will take care of it."
Motoki gave me her most dazzling smile...{p}

"Don't talk crap!
Why the hell would he come?!"
Shindo suddenly raised his voice.{p}

"...Oh?
Shindo, you know Kanda?"
Motoki put on a big show of surprise. Whether it was real or an act, I couldn't tell.{p}

"Don't talk crap!
Why the hell would he come?!"
Shindo suddenly raised his voice.{p}

"...Oh?
Shindo, you know Kanda?"
Motoki put on a big show of surprise. Whether it was real or an act, I couldn't tell.{p}

"Don't talk crap!
Why the hell would he come?!"
Shindo suddenly raised his voice.{p}

"...Oh?
Shindo, you know Kanda?"
Motoki put on a big show of surprise. Whether it was real or an act, I couldn't tell.{p}

"It wasn't a lie!
I wasn't lying when I said it."
I was practically shouting.{p}

I slowly opened my eyes.
Everyone else was cautiously looking around too.
What about Kazama★{p}

...What's going on?
Did Kazama save us from Kanda?
Wasn't Kazama just a weirdo?{p}

"Kanda☆
It's you, Kanda, isn't it?
Why are you here?"{p}

(S-stop... Quit it!)
Kanda thrashed about, twisting his body to get the head off, but it didn't seem to be working.
It looked as though he had lost control of his body.{p}

Then Motoki gripped my hand tightly.
"It's okay. I'll protect you."
It was all over.{p}

(Fuku...)
Before I could even answer in my head, Kanda's reply came back.
(...Understood. {b} {a}, then.){p}

Then Kanda came walking stiffly into the club room.
At this rate, my life really was in danger.
Everyone had their eyes shut, praying with all their might.{p}

"That's right, {a}.
I came here to save you, after all."
Urk...!{p}

At the corners of her mouth, the faces of countless people were writhing.
Was she telling me to become one of them...?
So that's what she meant by saving me...{p}
